SUMMARY:ART TALKS – Beyond The Gallery: Art\, Community and Connection wi
 th Katherine Kemp and Colin Bushell
DESCRIPTION:[vc_row css=”.vc_custom_1523319263370{padding-top: 20px !impo
 rtant\;padding-bottom: 30px !important\;}”][vc_column][vc_column_text] F
 or our next ‘ART TALKS’ event\, the Royal Queensland Art Society Brisb
 ane Branch invites its members and the art loving community to: “Beyond 
 The Gallery: Art\, Community and Connection” In this presentation and Q&
 A\, Katherine Kemp and Colin Bushell\, co-founders of Art & Eats\, will ex
 amine how they have drawn upon local energy to break down community barrie
 rs and build a creative ecosystem\, not just an exhibition. They share the
 ir successes\, the pitfalls and future vision\, providing advice on buildi
 ng a model others can follow. Art & Eats delivers the principle of showcas
 ing creativity\, whilst bringing together community beyond the gallery. Th
 ey believe in partnership before ownership and purpose before profit. Kath
 erine is the owner of Ruby Red Jewellery and co-founder of Art & Eats. She
  is also a Jewellery designer\, small-business owner\, entrepreneur\, valu
 er\, gemologist and MBA recipient. Colin runs Colin Bushell Photography an
 d is co-founder of Art & Eats with Katherine. He is also a multi-award-win
 ning photographer\, writer and photojournalist\; co-founder and former Pre
 sident of The Gap Creative\; former Vice President\, Professional Photogra
 phers’ Association of Queensland. This talk will be held at RQAS Brisban
 e Gallery on Sunday\, 20th of September from 2pm to 4pm . Afternoon tea is
  included in the ticket price. Ticket Prices: – $5 for RQAS Brisbane Mem
 bers – $15 for the Public Don’t miss your chance to attend this month
 ’s art talks event and enjoy the fellowship of other like-minded artists
  – book your tickets via the link below now! Please note this event will
  be held in the main gallery space which is wheelchair accessible. [/vc_co
