BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-d2ul5w@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260924T183000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260924T203000
SUMMARY:The Explainer Series: Supermarkets
DESCRIPTION:The Explainer Series is about exploring the questions we’re a
 ll asking.Supermarkets are part of everyday life\, but there’s a lot mor
 e happening in the aisles than deciding what’s for dinner. From pricing 
 and loyalty programs to store layouts\, online shopping and the growing in
 fluence of AI\, the way we buy our groceries is changing fast. The Explain
 er Series: Supermarkets will take a look behind the shelves to explore how
  Australian supermarkets became the giants they are today - and where they
  might be heading next. As smaller stores\, home delivery\, automated fulf
 illment and personalised shopping reshape the supermarket experience\, wha
 t do we gain from all that convenience\, and what might we be giving up? J
 oin us as we unpack the power and psychology of supermarkets\, the technol
 ogy changing the way we shop\, and what the supermarket of the future migh
 t look like.
LOCATION:State Library of Queensland\, Stanley Place\, South Bank
URL:https://www.slq.qld.gov.au/whats-on/explainer-series-supermarkets
END:VEVENT
