BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-1c36caa@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260916T120000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20261003T160000
SUMMARY:Geoffrey Burns: Ride the Chronovore
DESCRIPTION:Revisiting locations at different times of year\, Geoffrey Burn
 s approaches making as both a method and a measure of time. Works emerge t
 hrough repeated encounters with place\, where observation accumulates and 
 memory takes form through surface and seasonal change. Ride the Chronovore
  considers time as an active force: consuming\, transforming and leaving i
 ts evidence behind. Through repetition\, Burns traces how surfaces shift\,
  forms appear and recede\, and environments register cycles that often unf
 old beyond human attention. Each return gathers new information while reve
 aling what has altered\, disappeared or endured. The fleeting span of a hu
 man life meets the slower tempo of the natural world\, inviting an attenti
 ve and materially grounded way of looking at the quiet force of time. Open
 ing Night Friday September 18 6 - 8pm VIP Preview from 5.30pm Geoffrey Bur
 ns in Conversation Sunday September 20 3pm - 4pm + celebratory drinks with
  the artist until 5pm Artist in Residence Saturday September 26 12pm - 4pm
  (drop in any time) Morning Musings Workshop Retreat Sunday October 4 10am
  - 12pm
LOCATION:PARKER Contemporary\, 38 Hope Street
URL:https://www.parkercontemporary.com.au/exhibitions/geoffrey-burns
END:VEVENT
