SUMMARY:Audrey Gibbs Art Prize
DESCRIPTION:[vc_row css=”.vc_custom_1523319263370{padding-top: 20px !impo
 rtant\;padding-bottom: 30px !important\;}”][vc_column][vc_column_text]Au
 drey Gibbs joined the Royal Queensland Art Society in 1983 and was recogni
 sed as a Fellow of the society in 2009. This exhibition explores genre art
 works\, one of Audrey’s great pleasures. Sponsored by the Gibbs family\,
  it will also feature a retrospective of some of her works. Genre Artworks
  are those that depict ordinary people in everyday situations\, both in th
 e exterior and the interior. Rather than heroic or mythological subjects\,
  these works celebrate the familiar: everyday people participating in dome
 stic routines\, work\, leisure\, social gatherings\, and quiet moments of 
 daily life. Spanning centuries\, the show highlights how artists have foun
 d beauty\, humour\, and meaning in the ordinary\, offering intimate window
 s into human experience and social history. Artists are invited to submit 
 artworks in their own choice of media including both 2D and 3D works.[/vc_
 column_text][vc_separator][/vc_column][/vc_row][vc_row css=”.vc_custom_1
 523319263370{padding-top: 20px !important\;padding-bottom: 30px !important
 \;}”][vc_column width=”1/3″][vc_single_image image=”25724″ img_s
 ize=”medium” alignment=”center” onclick=”img_link_large”][/vc_
 column][vc_column width=”1/3″][vc_single_image image=”25722″ img_s
 ize=”medium” alignment=”center” onclick=”img_link_large”][vc_c
 olumn_text] Examples of Audrey Gibbs work [/vc_column_text][/vc_column][vc
 _column width=”1/3″][vc_single_image image=”25720″ img_size=”med
 ium” alignment=”center” onclick=”img_link_large”][/vc_column][/v
 c_row][vc_row][vc_column][vc_single_image image=”26083″ img_size=”fu
 ll”][vc_column_text] On Saturday\, 3rd of October from 2pm \, join us at
  RQAS Brisbane Gallery for the Opening Event and prize presentation for th
 e inaugural Audrey Gibbs Art Prize! For this event nibbles will be provide
 d and drinks available for purchase. There will also be live music! We loo
 k forward to seeing you at the gallery for an enjoyable evening of art\, n
 ibbles and drinks\, and to be the first to hear the prize presentations. T
 icket prices: RQAS Brisbane Branch Members: $5 Non-Members: $15 Make sure 
 to secure your ticket via the link below soon as numbers are limited! Plea
 se note : This event will be held in the main gallery which is wheelchair 
 accessible.[/vc_column_text][vc_raw_html]JTNDJTIxLS0lMjBBZGQlMjB0aGUlMjBmb
 2xsb3dpbmclMjB0byUyMHlvdXIlMjB3ZWJzaXRlJTI3cyUyMEhUTUwuJTIwLS0lM0UlMEElM0N
 zY3JpcHQlMjBzcmMlM0QlMjJodHRwcyUzQSUyRiUyRmV2ZW50cy5odW1hbml0aXguY29tJTJGc
 2NyaXB0cyUyRndpZGdldHMlMkZpbmxpbmUuanMlMjIlMjB0eXBlJTNEJTIybW9kdWxlJTIyJTN
 FJTNDJTJGc2NyaXB0JTNFJTBBJTNDaWZyYW1lJTIwZGF0YS1jaGVja291dCUzRCUyMmF1ZHJle
 S1naWJicy1hcnQtcHJpemUtb3BlbmluZy1ldmVudCUyMiUzRSUzQyUyRmlmcmFtZSUzRQ==[/v
 c_raw_html][vc_separator][vc_column_text] ABOUT AUDREY GIBBS Audrey Gibbs 
 (1921-2015) was a well- known and greatly loved Queensland artist\, whose 
 body of work remains cherished in many collections. She was born in Marybo
 rough and educated at Rockhampton Girls Grammar School. She loved drawing 
 from an early age and was privately tutored during her school years. After
  matriculating\, she worked in a commercial art studio in Brisbane. She ma
 rried soon after the Second World War and then reared six children. When h
 er fifth child was two\, Audrey returned to her art\, attending life class
 es with Melville Haysom. In 1978 she went on to study drawing and watercol
 our at Seven Hills College of Art. She joined the Pastel Society in 1980 a
 nd the Half Dozen Group and Royal Queensland Art Society (RQAS) in 1983. I
 n 2009 Audrey was made a Fellow of the RQAS\, in recognition of her signif
 icant contribution to RQAS and the arts in Queensland. She exhibited at Ar
 drossan Gallery (1986 and 1988)\, Riverhouse Gallery (1993 and 1995)\, as 
 well as many sell out shows in her own home at Chelmer. Her work became no
 ted for her masterful use of light and tonal values. Audrey’s chief fasc
 ination was for figures in interiors\, in any medium. Her oil and watercol
 our painting offer honest and moving depictions of all the things she love
 d\, places she had been\, and people she knew. Over the years she embraced
  various styles in her pursuit of the aesthetic\, yet her work has always 
 remained recognisably Audrey. [/vc_column_text][vc_separator][vc_column_te
 xt] INFORMATION FOR ARTISTS [/vc_column_text][vc_column_text] Click on the
  buttons below to view prizes\, event dates\, entry fees and terms and con
 ditions: [/vc_column_text][vc_tta_tabs shape=”square” spacing=”10″
  alignment=”center” active_section=”1″][vc_tta_section title=”EV
 ENT DATES” tab_id=”dates”][vc_column_text] DATES [/vc_column_text][v
